{title: 382 - O Day of Rest and Gladness}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #382 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 382}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]O day of rest [Cm/G]and [Ab]glad ness, [Bbm]Oday [Ab]of joy and light,
[Gdim]O balm [Ab]of [Cm/G]care [Ab]and sad ness, most [Cm/G]beautiful, [Bbm]most [Cm/G]bright;
[Ab]On thee, the high and [Bb7]lowly, [Fm/C]who [Ab]bend before [Bbm]the [Ab]throne,
[Db/Ab]Sing, "Holy, [Bbm]holy, [Gdim]ho [Fm]ly," to [Ab]the [Bbm]Eter [Db/Ab]nal [Gdim]One.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Thou art [Cm/G]a [Ab]port [Cm/G]protected
[Ab]from storms [Cm/G]that [Bbm]round [Ab]us rise;
[Gdim]a [Ab]garden intersected
[Gdim]with [Ab]streams of paradise;
[Ab]thou art a [Eb/Bb]cooling [Ab]fountain
[Ab]in life's [Eb/Bb]dry, [Fm/C]dreary [Bbm]sand;
[Db/Ab]from [Gdim]thee, [Bbm]like [Fm]Pisgah's [Bbm]mountain,
[Db/Ab]we [Bbm]view [Gdim]our [Fm]promised [Db/Ab]land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]A day [Cm/G]of [Ab]sweet [Cm/G]reflection,
[Ab]thou art [Cm/G]a [Bbm]day [Ab]of love,
[Gdim]A [Ab]day to raise [Cm/G]affection
[Gdim]from [Ab]earth to things above.
[Ab]New graces [Eb/Bb]ever [Ab]gaining
[Ab]from this [Bb7]our [Fm/C]day [Ab]of [Bbm]rest,
[Db/Ab]We [Gdim]reach [Bbm]the [Fm]rest remaining
[Db/Ab]in [Bbm]mansions [Fm]of [Bbm]the [Db/Ab]blessed.
{end_of_verse}
